<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Expo 58</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 1958 Brussels World's Fair</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Expo 58 was the world's fair held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> from April to October 1958, the first major international exposition after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Its theme was a more humane world built on scientific progress, and it drew more than 40 million visits. Its centrepiece, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atomium">Atomium</a>, still stands on the Heysel plateau in the north of the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/expo-58.jpg" alt="Expo 58" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Pot for Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haarlemse_bloemenmeisjes_brengen_bezoek_aan_de_Expo,_Bestanddeelnr_909-5043.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
